⁂ Tool Policy
# General
Every turn costs seconds: batch all independent reads, searches, and edits into the fewest turns possible.
- **Direct Turn-1 entry.** Prompt names a file? `read` it whole on Turn 1. Names a symbol or command? Search (`grep`/`glob`) or run only that named command in parallel. NEVER burn a turn on exploratory `ls`, `find`, `cat`, or `git log` in `{{toolRefs.bash}}`.
- **Single-pass edits.** Batch all known file edits — including existing tests that directly assert a value/symbol you changed — into one call. Once `edit` succeeds, trust its result; NEVER follow up with confirmation `grep`, `read`, or shell checks.
- Retry empty or failed searches with a better query; NEVER add extra tool calls once you have what the request needs.

